      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "For outdoor work, an aggressive approach with iodine soak is certainly stronger than soap and water, but a heavy, airtight seal is still risky for a deep puncture. Instead, use a thick layer of antibiotic ointment followed by a heavy-duty, waterproof, yet flexible bandage to protect against dirt while still allowing some surface drainage. You must monitor it closely, and if you notice any increased pain or warmth, you must stop working and seek professional care immediately.",
      "source": "target",
